        "**Project: Single-Cell RNA-seq Analysis Pipeline Using Python (Scanpy)**"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "pjXnh0rBbG0Q"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) is a modern sequencing technology that measures gene expression at the level of individual cells. Unlike traditional RNA sequencing, which provides the average gene expression across thousands of cells, scRNA-seq analyzes each cell separately. This allows researchers to identify different cell types, discover rare cell populations, study disease mechanisms, and understand cellular diversity.\n",
        "\n",
        "To analyze scRNA-seq data, we need specialized bioinformatics software. One of the most widely used Python libraries for this purpose is Scanpy."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Pw74WAGBFRiY"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Step 1: Install Scanpy**\n",
        "\n",
        "**What is Scanpy?**\n",
        "\n",
        "Scanpy is an open-source Python library designed specifically for analyzing single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) data. It provides a complete workflow from reading raw data to generating biological insights.\n",
        "\n",
        "With Scanpy, researchers can:\n",
        "\n",
        "Import single-cell datasets    \n",
        "Perform quality control (QC)                \n",
        "Normalize gene expression data     \n",
        "Identify highly variable genes                          \n",
        "Perform dimensionality reduction (PCA)    \n",
        "Cluster similar cells\n",
        "Visualize data using UMAP and t-SNE  \n",
        "Identify marker genes for different cell types\n",
        "\n",
        "Scanpy is widely used in bioinformatics research because it is fast, scalable, and capable of handling datasets containing millions of cells."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "DZ47h4sCFVd_"
      }
