        "**Step 3: Download an Example scRNA-seq Dataset (PBMC 3K)**\n",
        "\n",
        "**Introduction**\n",
        "\n",
        "Before we can analyze single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) data, we need a dataset. A dataset is a structured collection of biological information. In scRNA-seq, a dataset contains the gene expression values of thousands of individual cells.\n",
        "\n",
        "For beginners, downloading and preparing real scRNA-seq datasets from public databases such as GEO or 10x Genomics can be complicated because they often require multiple files, decompression, and preprocessing.\n",
        "\n",
        "To make learning easier, Scanpy provides built-in example datasets that can be downloaded with a single line of Python code. One of the most popular example datasets is the PBMC 3K dataset."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "nkC5nZleITPb"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "What is PBMC?\n",
        "\n",
        "PBMC stands for Peripheral Blood Mononuclear Cells.\n",
        "\n",
        "These are immune cells found in human blood that have a single round nucleus (mononuclear).\n",
        "\n",
        "PBMCs are widely used in biomedical research because they play important roles in the immune system.\n",
        "\n",
        "Common PBMC cell types include:\n",
        "\n",
        "T cells    \n",
        "B cells    \n",
        "Natural Killer (NK) cells  \n",
        "Monocytes  \n",
        "Dendritic cells"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "TL52PQn6JWzq"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "import scanpy as sc\n",
        "\n",
        "adata = sc.datasets.pbmc3k()\n",
        "\n",
        "adata"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6SvD6jyKbxxa"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Step 4: View Data**\n",
        "\n",
        "Think of it like opening a new Excel file before analyzing it—you first look at the rows, columns, and values to understand what information is available."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "BrJLIixsK57B"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "PezVJcbsJVpQ"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "adata.obs.head()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "zKlOExNDb8Eh"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Step 5: Quality Control (QC)\n",
        "Introduction **bold text**\n",
        "\n",
        "After loading the single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) dataset, the next and one of the most important steps is Quality Control (QC).\n",
        "\n",
        "Quality Control is the process of checking the quality of the sequencing data before performing biological analysis.\n",
        "\n",
        "If low-quality cells remain in the dataset, they can produce incorrect clustering, misleading gene expression patterns, and inaccurate biological conclusions."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "mY8HgSbkL4p-"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "sc.pp.calculate_qc_metrics(\n",
        "    adata,\n",
        "    inplace=True\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "hIZ2OS_fb-sr"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Step 6: Visualize QC Metrics**\n",
        "\n",
        "This creates a violin plot showing the distribution of detected genes across all cells.\n",
        "\n",
        "This function creates a violin plot.\n",
        "\n",
        "A violin plot shows:\n",
        "\n",
        "Distribution of data\n",
        "Density of values\n",
        "Median\n",
        "Spread of observations\n",
        "\n",
        "It is similar to a box plot but provides more information about how the data are distributed."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "exLiD5g5Pbnw"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "sc.pl.violin(\n",
        "    adata,\n",
        "    ['n_genes_by_counts'],\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "jNO25xp6b_3u"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Step 7: Filter Low Quality Cells\n",
        "\n",
        "This process is called filtering.\n",
        "\n",
        "Filtering means selecting only the cells that meet specific quality criteria and removing cells that are likely to produce unreliable results.in scRNA-seq analysis, we remove poor-quality cells before continuing with normalization, clustering, and downstream analysis."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ZNmbSxIiRErH"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "adata = adata[\n",
        "    adata.obs.n_genes_by_counts > 200\n",
        "]\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "MHZFVr3JcGd6"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Step 8: Normalize Data**\n",
        "\n",
        "What is Normalization?\n",
        "\n",
        "Normalization is the process of changing numerical values to a common scale so that no feature dominates because of its larger numbers.\n",
        "\n",
        "In simple words:\n",
        "\n",
        "Normalization means converting different-sized numbers into a similar range so the machine learning model can compare them fairly."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "oFWYaM-QSd69"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "sc.pp.normalize_total(\n",
        "    adata,\n",
        "    target_sum=10000\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "sc.pp.log1p(adata)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "mcNNDN6NcJOe"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Step 9: Find Important Genes**\n",
        "\n",
        "This Scanpy function calculates which genes show the most variation across cells."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5reFEFI5WQIu"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(\n",
        "    adata,\n",
        "    n_top_genes=2000\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ioCzqdMicLTx"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "adata = adata[:, adata.var.highly_variable]"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "OQGBLQCbcNLn"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Step 10: PCA** (Principal Component Analysis)\n",
        "\n",
        "PCA is used to reduce the complexity of gene expression data while keeping the most important biological information."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "hcEVY2WeYOh6"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "sc.pp.scale(adata)\n",
        "\n",
        "sc.tl.pca(adata)\n",
        "\n",
        "sc.pl.pca_variance_ratio(adata)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "yH_w8-vicOxk"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Step 11: Clustering**\n",
        "\n",
        "Which cells are similar to each other and can be grouped into the same cell type?\n",
        "\n",
        "This process is called clustering."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "i6uZ_fVxYaf3"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "sc.pp.neighbors(\n",
        "    adata,\n",
        "    n_neighbors=10,\n",
        "    n_pcs=20\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "wW-l9ohNcQnQ"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "sc.tl.leiden(\n",
        "    adata,\n",
        "    resolution=0.5\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "XQmuEB-gcSOg"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "adata.obs['leiden'].value_counts()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8-W9X4VxcU_3"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Step 12: UMAP Visualization**\n",
        "\n",
        "Convert high-dimensional single-cell data into a simple 2D map that humans can visualize.Converts complex high-dimensional data into a 2D picture."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "U-kp6coxYwPv"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "sc.tl.umap(adata)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Xf1zT53OcXGZ"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "sc.pl.umap(\n",
        "    adata,\n",
        "    color=\"leiden\"\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "hYGOMmXmcYPR"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Step 13: Find Marker Genes**\n",
        "\n",
        "Marker genes are genes that identify a cell type."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "dQheOpA2Y1gH"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "sc.tl.rank_genes_groups(\n",
        "    adata,\n",
        "    groupby=\"leiden\",\n",
        "    method=\"wilcoxon\"\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "NW_J1zpgcbu6"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "sc.pl.rank_genes_groups(\n",
        "    adata,\n",
        "    n_genes=10\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "CUH6gtMJcdYJ"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
